# Cloudflare Pages response headers.
#
# WHY THIS EXISTS
# Pages serves HTML with max-age=0 but static assets with max-age=14400 (4h).
# That split means a deploy can land the new markup while the browser -- or any
# proxy between it and the edge, including a filtering DNS/HTTP appliance --
# keeps serving the previous CSS and JS for hours. The symptom is a site that
# looks half-updated: current copy, stale styling and stale behaviour, and any
# newly added stylesheet rule silently missing.
#
# no-cache does NOT mean "don't store". It means "store, but revalidate before
# reusing". Responses still 304 when nothing changed, so repeat loads stay cheap
# while a deploy takes effect immediately.
#
# Pages matches these patterns against the path only. A suffix pattern like
# /*.css is NOT matched, so the rule has to be a prefix splat: everything
# revalidates, then the directories whose files change name when they change
# get a long cache back.

/*
  Cache-Control: no-cache

/assets/img/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=604800

/assets/icons/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=604800

/assets/audio/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=604800

/games/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=86400
